// CKF Hard Mode — rule set and syntax tutorial
//
// Copy to: <game>/BepInEx/config/ckf.hardmode.rules.json
// The engine skips // comments and allows trailing commas, so this file can
// stay readable.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SYNTAX
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   "model"     which table to hook, e.g. "WeaponModel" (the "Model" suffix
//               is optional — "Weapon" also works)
//   "comment"   free text, ignored by the engine
//
//   MATCHING (omit all of them to match every row):
//   "where"     exact equality. Numbers, strings and booleans.
//   "whereMin"  column >= value
//   "whereMax"  column <= value
//   All conditions must pass for the rule to apply (they AND together).
//
//   OPERATIONS (applied in this order):
//   "set"       assign an absolute value
//   "multiply"  scale the current value
//   "add"       offset the current value (use negatives to subtract)
//   "clampMin"  raise to a floor — never lowers
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE THREE RULES THAT WILL BITE YOU
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Match on the DOMAIN id, not "Id". WeaponModel.Id is read-only and -1.
//    Use WeaponId / ArmorId / TalentId.
//
// 2. Weapon combat stats live in TWO firing-mode blocks suffixed 1 and 2.
//    Unsuffixed Accuracy / PureDamage / BallisticDamage / ActionPoints are
//    READ-ONLY aliases for the active mode — writing to them does nothing.
//
// 3. Talent "Adjusted*" columns are READ-ONLY. Write ApCost, Range,
//    MaxCharges, RechargeTurns instead.
//
// 4. A talent is spread across THREE tables. TalentModel holds the base
//    stats (cost, range, cooldown, duration). EffectModel holds the numbers
//    the talent actually hands out (AP granted, evasion, heals, crit
//    vulnerability). JobNodeModel holds the per-tier upgrade deltas, keyed by
//    JobNodeId. Retuning "the talent" usually means touching more than one.
//    See docs/talent-upgrade-nodes.md.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPOUNDING — read this before touching GameMonsterModel
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DataDb models (Weapon, Armor, Talent) are re-materialized fresh from the
// content database on every read, so "multiply" applies exactly once per
// object. Safe.
//
// GameDb models (anything starting Game*, like GameMonsterModel) come from
// your SAVE. If the game writes the row back and re-reads it later, a
// "multiply" applies AGAIN on top of the already-modified value and runs away.
// For Game* models prefer "set" and "clampMin", which are idempotent.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ID CHEATSHEET (verified against StreamingAssets/Locales/en-US.json)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   WeaponId  1013  EagleSight            |  3 Bull Assault, 17 Raikon AR12
//   WeaponId 20000  Guard Rifle Lvl1      |  20001-20005 Lvl2-Lvl6 (enemy range)
//   ArmorId      5  SecurTek Lightsuit    |  6 SecurTek Flex, 9 GX-Mesh
//   TalentId   100  Security Scramble     |  1 Any Grenade, 3 Any Combat Drug
// Locale keys are WeaponName.<id>, ArmorName.<id>, Talent.Name.<id>.
//
// GEAR LIVES IN ckf.hardmode.d/, NOT HERE.  122 rules were lifted out on
// 2026-08-25 and re-expressed as CSV overlays, carrying the exact values these
// rules produced — see overlays/_reference/rules-removed.json for the originals
// and overlays/README.md for why.  Adding an ArmorModel or WeaponModel rule
// here still works, but it will fight the overlays, which load after this file
// and win.  Put gear numbers in the CSVs.
//
// Enemy gear is gone from this file.  PLAYER-directed gear rules stayed and are
// prefixed "PLAYER" in their comment — keep that prefix, and add it to any new
// player gear rule, and the generator will leave it here.
